    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Sulphuric Acid used in Metallurgy, Smelting, Brass & Tinplate: McCulloch (1880), Dictionary of Commerce, scan p. 85"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Used in soldering and galvanising iron, with iron filings as cement for iron, &c. Sulphate of Ammonia.—It is procured from gas liquor in same manner as the chloride, by substituting sulphuric acid for muriatic."@en ;
